   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Run R&#39;s <b>parse </b>function on script.R. That should tell you what the parse error is. (Arguably, packrat should show you this error; I&#39;ve opened issue #36 to suggest that it should.) Once the file parses successfully, you should be able to bootstrap the directory without problems.<div><br></div><div>If you&#39;re seeing problems even after resolving parse errors, here are a couple of next steps:</div><div><br></div><div>1) You can indeed add dependencies manually. Do this by creating a &quot;dependencies.R&quot; file in your project directory and adding a require(<i>libraryname</i>) statement for each dependency.</div><div>2) If you&#39;re willing, post the file that parses in R but not in packrat here so we can investigate further. </div><div><div><br></div><div>Jonathan.</div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
