"color:#066\">4.1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span style=\"color:#000\">     <br>rpart</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">plot     </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#000\">     <br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">RWeka</span><span style=\"color:#000\">          </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">21</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    <br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">RWekajars</span><span style=\"color:#000\">      </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3.7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  <br>scales         </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#000\">     <br>stringr        </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#000\">     <br>survival       </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2.37</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    <br>texreg         </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.30</span><span style=\"color:#000\">      <br>vcd            </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\">     <br><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Fetching</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sources </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> abind </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">...</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> OK </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">CRAN current</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Errore</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> getSourceForPkgRecord</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">pkgRecord</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sourceDir</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> availablePkgs</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> repos</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>  </span><span style=\"color:#606\">No</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sources available </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">package</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> boot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Packrat</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> can find sources </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> packages on CRAN</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">like repositories </span><span style=\"color:#008\">and</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> packages <br>installed </span><span style=\"color:#008\">using</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> devtools</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span style=\"color:#000\">install_github</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">For</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> other </span><span style=\"color:#008\">package</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> types</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> supply the path to the </span><span style=\"color:#008\">package</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;s source using <br>the argument sourcePackagePaths = c(&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#080\">/path/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">to</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">package1</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;, &#39;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">path</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">to</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">package2</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;, ...)<br>Inoltre: Warning message:<br>In inferPackageRecord(df) : Couldn&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#000\">t figure </span><span style=\"color:#008\">out</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> the origin of </span><span style=\"color:#008\">package</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> boot<br></span></div></code></div><br><br><br>Package boot is available on CRAN, so I don&#39;t see why I get this message. Anyway, I used the option suggested:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> packrat</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span style=\"color:#000\">snapshot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sourcePackagePaths</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;/Library/Frameworks/R.framework/Versions/3.0/Resources/library/boot&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>In this way I got it to work, but if I delete the library folder the initPackrat() command won&#39;t work.<br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> initPackrat</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Initializing</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> packrat</span><span style=\"color:#660\">...</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> OK<br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Installing</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> abind </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">...</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> OK </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">downloaded binary</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Installing</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> boot </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">9</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">...</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sh</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">/usr/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bin</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">gnutar</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">No</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> such file </span><span style=\"color:#008\">or</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> directory<br>sh</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">/usr/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bin</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">gnutar</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">No</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> such file </span><span style=\"color:#008\">or</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> directory<br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Errore</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> system</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">cmd</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> intern </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> error </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> running command<br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Inoltre</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Warning</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> message</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">In</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> untar</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">src</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> exdir </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> target</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> compressed </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;gzip&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">‘/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">usr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bin</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">gnutar </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">xf </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;/Users/rhobis/Copy/Universita/LM_ScienzeStatistiche/SecondoAnno/DataMining/EsameFinale/prova4/packrat.sources/boot/boot_1.3-9.tar.gz&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">C </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;/var/folders/jl/s4bxtlkj2c92tsh9zddstqdr0000gn/T//RtmpveGOuE&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">’</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> returned error code </span><span style=\"color:#066\">127</span></div></code></div><br><br><br>Roberto<br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "SSTX8td9RFMJ",
   "from": "Jonathan McPherson",
   "author": "5893d17d64b5b0c2",
   "date": "2013-12-31T16:52:20Z",
   "subject": "Re: bootstrap issue: Failed to parse",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">On OSX Mavericks, R will sometimes try to use /usr/bin/gnutar, which was dropped in Mavericks. This appears to be the source of both of the errors you&#39;re seeing. You can fix the problem by telling R to use /usr/bin/tar instead. Put this in the .Renviron:<div><br></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(58,81,106);font-family:&#39;Segoe UI&#39;,&#39;Lucida Grande&#39;,Tahoma,Helvetica;line-height:18px\">TAR=/usr/bin/tar</span><br></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(58,81,106);font-family:&#39;Segoe UI&#39;,&#39;Lucida Grande&#39;,Tahoma,Helvetica;line-height:18px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(58,81,106);font-family:&#39;Segoe UI&#39;,&#39;Lucida Grande&#39;,Tahoma,Helvetica;line-height:18px\">Jonathan.</span></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "eULy1bpuWV0J",
   "from": "Rhobis",
   "author": "a8cefff212269182",
   "date": "2014-01-05T12:04:24Z",
   "subject": "Re: bootstrap issue: Failed to parse",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I found in the Revinron file this: <br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">TAR</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">$</span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TAR</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;/usr/bin/gnutar&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>and i replaced it with:<br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">TAR</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">$</span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TAR</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;/usr/bin/tar&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span></div></code></div><br><br>Now it seems to work, it still gives me that issue with the boot library, but it works using:<br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">packrat</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bootstrap</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sourcePackagePaths</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;/Library/Frameworks/R.framework/Versions/3.0/Resources/library/boot&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><br><br>Thank you very much for your help,<br>Roberto.<br><br><br><br><br><br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
}
